                    "description": {
                      "value": "However you acquired and used your piloting skills, your love of jumpships has led you to spend a great deal of time in space. You cannot become disoriented in microgravity or zero-gravity conditions. Your familiarity with interplanetary traffic and typical flight paths enables you to avoid certain unnatural hazards of space travel, like pirates and other ship-based attackers. Whether or not you own a jumpship of your own, your connections to other pilots probably enable you to find a ship in a pinch (at your Architect's discretion)."
